{"parentUuid":"4b9d27ef-df95-4928-a8c6-3721452587d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatgJafKNKrmLs4gye3Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"R6 compiles for every operation in K4's scope, and all 68 theorems stay within {propext, Quot.sound}. Committing step 3."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":546478,"output_tokens":1741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1741,"cache_read_input_tokens":546478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1269f101-afd9-425b-ae0d-c02497a19f8e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgatgJDauwVLuoT5xqqvG","requestRef":"f56ca56c-c8ea-4ded-a9b8-c8beda9a7f73","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"04698ab6-317a-42ca-9858-f6ba066f2038","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:47:15.402Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"04698ab6-317a-42ca-9858-f6ba066f2038","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatgJafKNKrmLs4gye3Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CoHjycoUEdHhfCdACtCtdn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/MM23.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"/-! ## Smoke test -/\"\nadd='''/-- R6 for `exitFrame` on the reached states (MM-03.3 §9.2, §10), under `DDSound k`: `WF3` and\n`FrameOwnedLive` hold there. -/\ntheorem r6_exit_reachable {k : K} {statics : Statics} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop}\n    {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {tok : Nat → Nat} {L : Layout}\n    {s3 s3' : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hdd : DDSound k) (hr : Reachable k statics s3)\n    (hR : Repr tok L s3 s2) (htc : TokCompat C tok) (h : ExitStep k s3 (.ok s3')) :\n    AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (exitOps L tok s3) ∧ Repr tok L s3' (exec s2 (exitOps L tok s3)) :=\n  r6_exit (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1 (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).2 hR htc h\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, add+anchor)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -E \"warning|error|Build\" | head; cd .. && grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .; git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM23.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nMM23 pass 1, step 3: R6 for the operations in the scope of K4\n\nWhy: MM-03.3 §9.2 R6 asks that each concrete effect of a safe MM-03 step\nbe an authorised MM-02 transition; K4 fixes the correspondence.\n\nWhat:\n- r6_read3 (reads), r2_write3/r2_writeShared (writes, step 2).\n- r6_alloc: one-root shape (O14) -> one AllocStep at the placement;\n  r6_alloc_fail: no step, Repr kept.\n- r6_free: one DeallocStep of the root's allocation, under the contract\n  obligation FreeSound (FreeCompat -> MM-02 Compatible).\n- r6_enter: one AllocStep per root local with the new frame's token.\n- r6_exit (+ _reachable): one DeallocStep per root owned by the exited\n  frame, token compatible by construction (TokCompat); owned storage\n  that dies with the frame keeps a live allocation.\n- r6_noStep: derive, split, release, depend, endUse, pin, unpin,\n  newArena, reset map to no step and keep Repr.\n- Support: exists_leaf, rootAlloc, deallocOps, repr_deallocs,\n  Repr.shrink, exec_wf.\n\nHow proved: lake build clean; no sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide; the 69\ntheorems use at most propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Add the exit corollary, build, commit step 3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":546478,"output_tokens":1741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1741,"cache_read_input_tokens":546478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CoHjycoUEdHhfCdACtCtdn":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/MM23.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"/-! ## Smoke test -/\"\nadd='''/-- R6 for `exitFrame` on the reached states (MM-03.3 §9.2, §10), under `DDSound k`: `WF3` and\n`FrameOwnedLive` hold there. -/\ntheorem r6_exit_reachable {k : K} {statics : Statics} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop}\n    {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {tok : Nat → Nat} {L : Layout}\n    {s3 s3' : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hdd : DDSound k) (hr : Reachable k statics s3)\n    (hR : Repr tok L s3 s2) (htc : TokCompat C tok) (h : ExitStep k s3 (.ok s3')) :\n    AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (exitOps L tok s3) ∧ Repr tok L s3' (exec s2 (exitOps L tok s3)) :=\n  r6_exit (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1 (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).2 hR htc h\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, add+anchor)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -E \"warning|error|Build\" | head; cd .. && grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .; git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM23.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nMM23 pass 1, step 3: R6 for the operations in the scope of K4\n\nWhy: MM-03.3 §9.2 R6 asks that each concrete effect of a safe MM-03 step\nbe an authorised MM-02 transition; K4 fixes the correspondence.\n\nWhat:\n- r6_read3 (reads), r2_write3/r2_writeShared (writes, step 2).\n- r6_alloc: one-root shape (O14) -> one AllocStep at the placement;\n  r6_alloc_fail: no step, Repr kept.\n- r6_free: one DeallocStep of the root's allocation, under the contract\n  obligation FreeSound (FreeCompat -> MM-02 Compatible).\n- r6_enter: one AllocStep per root local with the new frame's token.\n- r6_exit (+ _reachable): one DeallocStep per root owned by the exited\n  frame, token compatible by construction (TokCompat); owned storage\n  that dies with the frame keeps a live allocation.\n- r6_noStep: derive, split, release, depend, endUse, pin, unpin,\n  newArena, reset map to no step and keep Repr.\n- Support: exists_leaf, rootAlloc, deallocOps, repr_deallocs,\n  Repr.shrink, exec_wf.\n\nHow proved: lake build clean; no sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide; the 69\ntheorems use at most propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Add the exit corollary, build, commit step 3"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01CoHjycoUEdHhfCdACtCtdn":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devla