{"parentUuid":"ce4c99c5-38d2-485d-986f-bf8a40e13ee9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06503e62-b7bb-46dd-8bf0-90c46d6d2b97","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vqaa79otQS2wBSZCrVFvYj","type":"tool_result","content":"1802:/-! ## Smoke test -/\n1803-\n1804-namespace Smoke\n1805-\n1806-def st : Statics := [((none, none, 0), true)]\n1807-def L : Layout := fun _ => ⟨0, 0, 4⟩\n1808-def tk : Nat → Nat := fun f => 100 + f\n1809-def g : Nat → Geom := fun _ => ⟨0, 4, 4⟩\n1810-def w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat := fun l i => ((l + i).toUInt8, none)\n1811-/-- Obligations of the test cases: `dec` asks an access aligned on 4 bytes (K5: a non-trivial\n1812-instance); `stat` is true, as K5 fixes for the sequential fragment. -/\n1813-def obR : MM02.ReadOblSpec := ⟨fun _ ac => ac.addr % 4 = 0, fun _ _ => True⟩\n1814-def obW : MM02.WriteOblSpec := ⟨fun _ ac _ => ac.addr % 4 = 0, fun _ _ _ => True⟩\n1815-instance : ∀ s o, Decidable (Op2.Dec obR obW s o) := fun s o => by\n1816-  cases o <;> simp only [Op2.Dec, obR, obW] <;> infer_instance\n1817-def s2 : MM02.State := exec MM02.State.empty (initOps topPlacement g tk L w st)\n1818-\n1819-example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 :=\n1820-  (repr_init (C := fun _ _ => False) (ObR := obR) (ObW := obW) (by decide) topPlacement_ok\n1821-    (by decide) (by decide) (fun _ _ _ => trivial) (by decide)).2\n1822-example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 := by decide\n1823-example : ¬ Repr tk L (S3.init st)\n1824-    (exec MM02.State.empty (allocOps topPlacement g (some (tk 0)) MM02.State.empty [0])) := by\n1825-  decide\n1826-\n1827-/-- Counterexample kept (report, (f)): the draft `canRead3` does not ask the leaves read to be\n1828-usable (MM-03.3 O9.1). In a state outside the reached ones, where the static 0 is freed but its\n1829-root authority stays active, `read3` is `ok`, `Repr` holds, and the MM-02 read is `ub`: R1 needs\n1830-`NoDangling`. -/\n1831-def cx : S3 := { S3.init st with dead := fun _ => true, freed := fun _ => true }\n1832-def cx2 : MM02.State := s2.dealloc 0\n1833-example : Repr tk L cx cx2 := by decide\n1834-example : Read3Step 0 [0] cx (.ok cx) := .ok (by decide)\n1835-example : MM02.ReadStep obR (leafAcc cx2 L .read 0) cx2 .ub :=\n1836-  .ub fun ⟨h, _⟩ => absurd h (by decide)\n1837-example : ¬ NoDangling cx := fun h => h 0 _ rfl rfl 0 (by decide) 0 (by decide) (by decide)\n1838-\n1839-end Smoke\n1840-\n1841-end Ern.MM23","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"17c75538-ca37-4a98-a6be-e322f7bc2614","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:53:04.619Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1802:/-! ## Smoke test -/\n1803-\n1804-namespace Smoke\n1805-\n1806-def st : Statics := [((none, none, 0), true)]\n1807-def L : Layout := fun _ => ⟨0, 0, 4⟩\n1808-def tk : Nat → Nat := fun f => 100 + f\n1809-def g : Nat → Geom := fun _ => ⟨0, 4, 4⟩\n1810-def w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat := fun l i => ((l + i).toUInt8, none)\n1811-/-- Obligations of the test cases: `dec` asks an access aligned on 4 bytes (K5: a non-trivial\n1812-instance); `stat` is true, as K5 fixes for the sequential fragment. -/\n1813-def obR : MM02.ReadOblSpec := ⟨fun _ ac => ac.addr % 4 = 0, fun _ _ => True⟩\n1814-def obW : MM02.WriteOblSpec := ⟨fun _ ac _ => ac.addr % 4 = 0, fun _ _ _ => True⟩\n1815-instance : ∀ s o, Decidable (Op2.Dec obR obW s o) := fun s o => by\n1816-  cases o <;> simp only [Op2.Dec, obR, obW] <;> infer_instance\n1817-def s2 : MM02.State := exec MM02.State.empty (initOps topPlacement g tk L w st)\n1818-\n1819-example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 :=\n1820-  (repr_init (C := fun _ _ => False) (ObR := obR) (ObW := obW) (by decide) topPlacement_ok\n1821-    (by decide) (by decide) (fun _ _ _ => trivial) (by decide)).2\n1822-example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 := by decide\n1823-example : ¬ Repr tk L (S3.init st)\n1824-    (exec MM02.State.empty (allocOps topPlacement g (some (tk 0)) MM02.State.empty [0])) := by\n1825-  decide\n1826-\n1827-/-- Counterexample kept (report, (f)): the draft `canRead3` does not ask the leaves read to be\n1828-usable (MM-03.3 O9.1). In a state outside the reached ones, where the static 0 is freed but its\n1829-root authority stays active, `read3` is `ok`, `Repr` holds, and the MM-02 read is `ub`: R1 needs\n1830-`NoDangling`. -/\n1831-def cx : S3 := { S3.init st with dead := fun _ => true, freed := fun _ => true }\n1832-def cx2 : MM02.State := s2.dealloc 0\n1833-example : Repr tk L cx cx2 := by decide\n1834-example : Read3Step 0 [0] cx (.ok cx) := .ok (by decide)\n1835-example : MM02.ReadStep obR (leafAcc cx2 L .read 0) cx2 .ub :=\n1836-  .ub fun ⟨h, _⟩ => absurd h (by decide)\n1837-example : ¬ NoDangling cx := fun h => h 0 _ rfl rfl 0 (by decide) 0 (by decide) (by decide)\n1838-\n1839-end Smoke\n1840-\n1841-end Ern.MM23","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ab2e1ce9-06c7-4162-b1b4-f621a81483fe","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce4c99c5-38d2-485d-986f-bf8a40e13ee9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
