{"parentUuid":"afb5d4ec-0223-41be-ad8f-f8ce2a2f88ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgauHk3L7X9TDwYSqpjjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed all 146 theorem constants rely only on {propext, Quot.sound}, and step 6 is committed (1f98afe). Now launching two background reviewers—one checking Repr against K1–K3, the other checking theorem statements against K4/K5—while I draft the report.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"output_tokens":4613,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1201},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4613,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"7aa2728e-e16c-4b55-9412-ad6c066d899c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgauHjiFLpAYTUkMQtJTc","requestRef":"666aa57f-ccea-4f86-b546-ce3d77b240d8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b3cbaa1-0dab-470d-9322-ba37d6476328","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:55:25.390Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"3b3cbaa1-0dab-470d-9322-ba37d6476328","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgauHk3L7X9TDwYSqpjjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016QCfyU7np4xkxKPzxGhzzF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial review of Repr","prompt":"You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (no Mathlib, Lean core v4.35). Do not modify any file in the repository. You may create scratch Lean files ONLY under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review_repr/ and check them with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>` (the module is built; start scratch files with `import Ern.MM23` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23`). `lake` is not on PATH: use ~/.elan/bin/lake. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac.\n\nContext. The task brief (French) is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/task_mm23_p1.md — read it fully, especially arbitrages K1, K2, K3 (they are normative for this pass). Specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-02) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md (MM-03.3). Project rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The module under review is /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean; it imports the drafts formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (unchanged).\n\nYour lens: the representation relation `Repr` (structure `Repr tok L s3 s2`, with `LayoutWF`, `Layout`, `AllocP`, `FrameGone`, `tokOf`). The brief says: \"revue adverse centrée sur Repr (une relation trop faible rendrait R1, R2 et R6 vides : chaque théorème doit avoir un témoin où sa conclusion n'est pas triviale)\".\n\nCheck, with evidence:\n1. Is each clause of `Repr` exactly what K1/K2/K3 say — not stronger, not weaker? Compare clause by clause: LayoutWF (a)(b)(c)(d); K2 (root ↔ allocation, part ↔ sub-range, arena block, frame token \"compatible par construction\"); K3 (usable root → live; Init leaf → bytes initialised; dead by free or frame exit → dead; dead by endUse (owned storage not freed) → live). Pay attention to the author's choices: `k` dropped from the signature (brief writes `Repr k L s3 s2`), `tok` added, the `exited` clause restricted to roots directly owned by a popped frame, the `leaked` clause generalised to every place-owned, non-usable, non-freed root (justified by K4 on exitFrame and free), tokens only for frame-owned roots, injectivity of root allocations.\n2. Is `Repr` too weak anywhere, i.e. are there pairs (s3, s2) satisfying `Repr` where the MM-02 state misrepresents the MM-03 state in a way the K1–K3 text forbids, or that would make R1/R2/R6 hold trivially? Is it too strong, i.e. does it reject a pair that K1–K3 accept, or make some R6 statement impossible for legitimate reached states? Try to build concrete counterexamples with `decide` (Repr is decidable).\n3. Do the cases at the end of the file (namespaces CaseInit and Cases) really show non-trivial conclusions for R1, R2, R4, R6, exclusive_bytes, repr_init? Are the negative tests (\"each clause of Repr rejects a wrong MM-02 state\") actually discriminating the clause they claim?\n4. Any place where an interpretation was chosen silently where K1–K3 are unclear.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (line numbers), cause (formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect), and evidence (spec quote, Lean counterexample with the exact command output, or a precise argument). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Keep the report under 900 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"output_tokens":4613,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1201},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4613,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016QCfyU7np4xkxKPzxGhzzF":{"description":"Adversarial review of Repr","prompt":"You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (no Mathlib, Lean core v4.35). Do not modify any file in the repository. You may create scratch Lean files ONLY under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review_repr/ and check them with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>` (the module is built; start scratch files with `import Ern.MM23` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23`). `lake` is not on PATH: use ~/.elan/bin/lake. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac.\n\nContext. The task brief (French) is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/task_mm23_p1.md — read it fully, especially arbitrages K1, K2, K3 (they are normative for this pass). Specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-02) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md (MM-03.3). Project rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The module under review is /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean; it imports the drafts formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (unchanged).\n\nYour lens: the representation relation `Repr` (structure `Repr tok L s3 s2`, with `LayoutWF`, `Layout`, `AllocP`, `FrameGone`, `tokOf`). The brief says: \"revue adverse centrée sur Repr (une relation trop faible rendrait R1, R2 et R6 vides : chaque théorème doit avoir un témoin où sa conclusion n'est pas triviale)\".\n\nCheck, with evidence:\n1. Is each clause of `Repr` exactly what K1/K2/K3 say — not stronger, not weaker? Compare clause by clause: LayoutWF (a)(b)(c)(d); K2 (root ↔ allocation, part ↔ sub-range, arena block, frame token \"compatible par construction\"); K3 (usable root → live; Init leaf → bytes initialised; dead by free or frame exit → dead; dead by endUse (owned storage not freed) → live). Pay attention to the author's choices: `k` dropped from the signature (brief writes `Repr k L s3 s2`), `tok` added, the `exited` clause restricted to roots directly owned by a popped frame, the `leaked` clause generalised to every place-owned, non-usable, non-freed root (justified by K4 on exitFrame and free), tokens only for frame-owned roots, injectivity of root allocations.\n2. Is `Repr` too weak anywhere, i.e. are there pairs (s3, s2) satisfying `Repr` where the MM-02 state misrepresents the MM-03 state in a way the K1–K3 text forbids, or that would make R1/R2/R6 hold trivially? Is it too strong, i.e. does it reject a pair that K1–K3 accept, or make some R6 statement impossible for legitimate reached states? Try to build concrete counterexamples with `decide` (Repr is decidable).\n3. Do the cases at the end of the file (namespaces CaseInit and Cases) really show non-trivial conclusions for R1, R2, R4, R6, exclusive_bytes, repr_init? Are the negative tests (\"each clause of Repr rejects a wrong MM-02 state\") actually discriminating the clause they claim?\n4. Any place where an interpretation was chosen silently where K1–K3 are unclear.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (line numbers), cause (formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect), and evidence (spec quote, Lean counterexample with the exact command output, or a precise argument). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Keep the report under 900 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7aa2728e-e16c-4b55-9412-ad6c066d899c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgauHjiFLpAYTUkMQtJTc","requestRef":"666aa57f-ccea-4f86-b546-ce3d77b240d8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25d1fb99-045a-410a-bec7-494e1a9252f0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:55:39.511Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"25d1fb99-045a-410a-bec7-494e1a9252f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgauHk3L7X9TDwYSqpjjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WZVZchLKSETNtiA7yjSHvS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial review of R-theorems","prompt":"You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (no Mathlib, Lean core v4.35). Do not modify any file in the repository. You may create scratch Lean files ONLY under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review_thm/ and check them with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>` (the module is built; start scratch files with `import Ern.MM23` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23`). `lake` is not on PATH: use ~/.elan/bin/lake. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac.\n\nContext. The task brief (French) is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/task_mm23_p1.md — read it fully: arbitrages K1–K5 are normative, steps 1–6 define what must be proved. Specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-02; note §MM-02.B, C, D, H and the 'stat'/'dec' obligations) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md (MM-03.3; note O9–O14, O6, O7, §9.2). Project rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The module under review is /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean; it imports the drafts formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (unchanged).\n\nYour lens: the refinement theorems and their hypotheses: repr_init, r1_read3, r2_write3, r2_writeShared, r6_read3, r6_alloc, r6_alloc_fail, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_noStep, r4_no_dead_cover, exclusive_bytes, and the *_reachable corollaries, plus the support definitions they rely on (Op2, exec, Along/AllOk/DecAlong, leafAcc, readOps/writeOps/allocOps/deallocOps/exitOps/initOps, Placement/PlacementOK/topPlacement, NewLayout, FreeSound, TokCompat, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive).\n\nCheck, with evidence:\n1. Does each statement say what the brief asks (R1: ReadStep ok on each range, never ub, value = bytes; R2: WriteStep ok and Repr preserved; R6 per K4 operation with only ok outcomes and arrival states in Repr; R4; exclusive_bytes)? Not weaker: look for vacuous or unsatisfiable hypotheses, hypotheses that assume the conclusion, quantifiers that make a statement trivial, sequences of MM-02 operations that do not match K4 (e.g. exitFrame deallocating exactly the automatic allocations, none for owned storage; free with the authority auth; alloc one AllocStep; enterFrame one AllocStep per root local; no step for derive/split/release/depend/endUse/pin/unpin/newArena/reset).\n2. Is every added hypothesis justified by the spec text (e.g. NoDangling and FpLeaves for R1/R2 because the draft canRead3/canWrite3 lack the usability clause of O9.1/O10.1 and the draft WF3 lacks 'footprints are leaves'; FrameOwnedLive for exit; FreeSound as the FreeCompat obligation; TokCompat as 'compatible par construction'; one-root shapes for alloc per O14 'une nouvelle racine'; NewLayout; PlacementOK)? Are the claims that these hold on reached states actually proved (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive, *_reachable)?\n3. K5: is `dec` ever instantiated by True in a theorem (it must stay an explicit hypothesis), and is `stat` handled as 'true in the sequential fragment'?\n4. Is the claim in exclusive_bytes' docstring correct that the task's conditions (b active, b not descending from a) are not needed? Is the statement at least as strong as the task's?\n5. Could any theorem be made to say something false by instantiating its free parameters (e.g. pick L, g, pl, C, ObR, ObW adversarially) while all hypotheses hold? Try in Lean.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (line numbers), cause (formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect), and evidence (spec quote, Lean counterexample with exact command output, or precise argument). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Keep the report under 900 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"output_tokens":4613,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1201},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4613,"cache_read_input_tokens":604506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WZVZchLKSETNtiA7yjSHvS":{"description":"Adversarial review of R-theorems","prompt":"You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (no Mathlib, Lean core v4.35). Do not modify any file in the repository. You may create scratch Lean files ONLY under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review_thm/ and check them with `cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>` (the module is built; start scratch files with `import Ern.MM23` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23`). `lake` is not on PATH: use ~/.elan/bin/lake. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac.\n\nContext. The task brief (French) is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/task_mm23_p1.md — read it fully: arbitrages K1–K5 are normative, steps 1–6 define what must be proved. Specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-02; note §MM-02.B, C, D, H and the 'stat'/'dec' obligations) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md (MM-03.3; note O9–O14, O6, O7, §9.2). Project rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The module under review is /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean; it imports the drafts formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (unchanged).\n\nYour lens: the refinement theorems and their hypotheses: repr_init, r1_read3, r2_write3, r2_writeShared, r6_read3, r6_alloc, r6_alloc_fail, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_noStep, r4_no_dead_cover, exclusive_bytes, and the *_reachable corollaries, plus the support definitions they rely on (Op2, exec, Along/AllOk/DecAlong, leafAcc, readOps/writeOps/allocOps/deallocOps/exitOps/initOps, Placement/PlacementOK/topPlacement, NewLayout, FreeSound, TokCompat, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive).\n\nCheck, with evidence:\n1. Does each statement say what the brief asks (R1: ReadStep ok on each range, never ub, value = bytes; R2: WriteStep ok and Repr preserved; R6 per K4 operation with only ok outcomes and arrival states in Repr; R4; exclusive_bytes)? Not weaker: look for vacuous or unsatisfiable hypotheses, hypotheses that assume the conclusion, quantifiers that make a statement trivial, sequences of MM-02 operations that do not match K4 (e.g. exitFrame deallocating exactly the automatic allocations, none for owned storage; free with the authority auth; alloc one AllocStep; enterFrame one AllocStep per root local; no step for derive/split/release/depend/endUse/pin/unpin/newArena/reset).\n2. Is every added hypothesis justified by the spec text (e.g. NoDangling and FpLeaves for R1/R2 because the draft canRead3/canWrite3 lack the usability clause of O9.1/O10.1 and the draft WF3 lacks 'footprints are leaves'; FrameOwnedLive for exit; FreeSound as the FreeCompat obligation; TokCompat as 'compatible par construction'; one-root shapes for alloc per O14 'une nouvelle racine'; NewLayout; PlacementOK)? Are the claims that these hold on reached states actually proved (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive, *_reachable)?\n3. K5: is `dec` ever instantiated by True in a theorem (it must stay an explicit hypothesis), and is `stat` handled as 'true in the sequential fragment'?\n4. Is the claim in exclusive_bytes' docstring correct that the task's conditions (b active, b not descending from a) are not needed? Is the statement at least as strong as the task's?\n5. Could any theorem be made to say something false by instantiating its free parameters (e.g. pick L, g, pl, C, ObR, ObW adversarially) while all hypotheses hold? Try in Lean.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (line numbers), cause (formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect), and evidence (spec quote, Lean counterexample with exact command output, or precise argument). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Keep the report under 900 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7aa2728e-e16c-4b55-9412-ad6c066d899c","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgauHjiFLpAYTUkMQtJTc","requestRef":"666aa57f-ccea-4f86-b546-ce3d77b240d8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"06afef29-f710-45dc-b113-fd43c54c6232","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:55:55.752Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
