nd R6 does not cover that step.\n- **Justification:** O14 \"création d'une nouvelle racine\". But O14.1 says the shape is \"représentée comme les emplacements locaux d'enterFrame\", which allows forests. With K4's single `AllocStep` and the K2 rule that one root maps to one allocation, the multi-root case cannot be in `Repr`, so the restriction is necessary.\n- **Action:** the hypothesis is documented and the counterexample is kept. It still needs to appear in report (e)/(f) as a gap between O14 and the draft.\n\n### F4 — minor — `FreeSound` (l.1468–1470)\n- **Cause:** the hypothesis is stronger than needed.\n- **Issue:** it quantifies over every pair (p, auth) for which `K` gives `Deallocable` and `FreeCompat`. `r6_free` only uses `hfs p auth` for the place actually freed (l.1574).\n  - A `K` that also declares `FreeCompat q a'` for a frame local `q` falsifies `FreeSound` unless `C a' (tok f)` holds. Such a `q` can never be freed, since `OwnedRoot` fails for it.\n  - When that happens `r6_free` cannot be applied, even though its conclusion for `p` still holds.\n- **Also open:** nothing establishes or preserves `FreeSound` across the K4 steps; for example, `r6_alloc` leaves the token `fa` unconstrained. So §9.1.4 (\"justifier … `FreeCompat`\") is still open and belongs in report (d).\n\n### Checks that passed\n- **What each statement says:**\n  - **R1:** `ReadStep` is ok on each range, with value `al.bytesAt off len`, the bytes are `InitRange`, and the `ub` outcome is ruled out.\n  - **R2:** `WriteStep` is ok for any bytes `w`, and `Repr` holds afterwards.\n  - **R6 vs K4:** each MM-02 sequence matches K4:\n    - read/write: one access per leaf, with authority `.read` / `.write`, provenance `(L l).alloc`;\n    - `alloc`: exactly one `AllocStep`;\n    - `enterFrame`: one `AllocStep` per root local;\n    - `free`: one `DeallocStep` of `rootAlloc` with authority `auth`;\n    - `exitFrame`: one `DeallocStep` per frame-owned root, with `tok top`;\n    - `NoStep` has exactly the nine operations K4 lists.\n  - Because the `ok` and `ub` constructors have contradictory premises, `AllOk` excludes `ub` in every case.\n- **Added hypotheses:**\n  - `NoDangling` and `FpLeaves` make up for the usability clauses missing from the draft's `canRead3`/`canWrite3`/`WriteSharedPre` (O9.1, O10.1, O11.1) and for WF3 clause 4. The kept counterexample `cx` (l.1839–1845) shows R1 fails without `NoDangling`.\n  - `reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive` is proved by induction over all `Reachable` constructors, under `DDSound`.\n  - `TokCompat` matches K2's \"compatible par construction\".\n  - `PlacementOK` is `AllocPre`, and `topPlacement_ok` shows it can be met.\n  - `NewLayout` restates K1 (b)/(c) together with K2 for the new roots.\n  - `MM02.WF` is MM-02's domain condition (H.4).\n- **K5:** no theorem instantiates `dec`; `Op2.Dec` is `True` only for alloc/dealloc, which have no `dec`. `stat` appears only as a hypothesis that it holds everywhere. The test cases set `dec` to a real 4-byte alignment check and `stat` to `True`, as K5 allows.\n- **`exclusive_bytes`:** the docstring's claim is correct. By rule 1 of MM-03.3.5, an inactive `b` has no effective mode. An active descendant of `a` covering `l` makes `a`'s effective mode on `l` absent or `Observe` (rules 3 and 4), which contradicts `Modify`. `effective_exclusive` needs only I1 and `a ≠ b`, and different leaves are covered by `LayoutWF.disjoint`. The statement drops the \"active\" and \"not a descendant\" conditions and assumes only `LayoutWF`, not all of `Repr`, so it is at least as strong as the task asks.\n- **Adversarial instantiation:** since everything is proved, no instance can be false. Choosing `L`, `g`, `pl`, `C`, `ObR`, `ObW` badly only makes the explicit hypotheses (`PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `FreeSound`, `dec`) unsatisfiable. The `Cases` section gives non-trivial witnesses for every theorem, and each clause of `Repr` rejects a wrong MM-02 state (l.2075–2080).\n\nNot checked: whether `Repr` implies that the MM-02 state stays admissible (MM-02 `Inv`); the task does not ask for it."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":19,"turnIndex":48},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
