{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:28:07.214Z","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wdhczph0j</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_012HKPWBqkAEYKrfsbZxp85S</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdhczph0j.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Second targeted check of the report-verification fixes of MM23 (commit 332a8b3)\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"lens\":\"report\",\"id\":\"F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, Résultats principaux 3\",\"claim\":\"Point 3 now says the MM-03 hypotheses are proved on reached states, with no condition. They are proved only under `DDSound k`. Its list of open obligations ('Les autres restent des obligations ouvertes, voir (d) 4') leaves out `DDSound`, and (d) 4 does not list it either.\",\"evidence\":\"Report: 'Les hypothèses MM-03 (`WF3`, `NoDangling`, `FpLeaves`, `FrameOwnedLive`) sont prouvées sur les états atteints. Les autres restent des obligations ouvertes, voir (d) 4 : FreeSound, NewLayout, PlacementOK, TokCompat ; MM02.WF, dec et stat ; l'hypothèse « une racine »…'. (b) itself says 'valent sur tout état atteint sous `DDSound k`'. In the module, every reached-state result takes `(hdd : DDSound k)`: r1_read3_reachable (MM23.lean:1267), r2_write3_reachable (1278), r2_writeShared_reachable (1289), r6_exit_reachable (1764) and r4_no_dead_cover (1777). R4 has no hypothesis other than Reachable, Repr and DDSound. Spec MM-03.3 §8 (l.521): 'La réalisation de `DDSound` à partir de dispositions mémoire réelles fait partie du raffinement de MM-03 vers MM-02'. So the obligation stays open, and only (d) 6 mentions it ('`DDSound` réel … Hors périmètre'). Secondary: `I1`, a hypothesis of exclusive_bytes (MM23.lean:1799), is in neither the 'MM-03 proved' group nor the 'open' group.\",\"fix\":\"Write 'sont prouvées sur les états atteints sous `DDSound k`'. Add `DDSound` to the list of open obligations, pointing to (d) 6 or adding it to (d) 4. Optionally name `I1` with the MM-03 hypotheses proved on reached states.\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"The finding holds. Summary point 3 says the MM-03 hypotheses are \\\"prouvées sur les états atteints\\\" with no condition. Every reached-state result in the module takes `DDSound k` as an explicit hypothesis. The list of remaining open obligations in point 3, and (d) 4 which it points to, both leave out `DDSound`; it appears only in the (b) preamble and in (d) 6 (\\\"Hors périmètre\\\"). This is an overstatement of the same kind the 332a8b3 fixes were meant to remove. Mitigating: `DDSound` is not hidden, since (b) and (d) 6 state it, so the defect is confined to the summary and the obligation list. That supports calling it major-to-minor rather than blocking. I did not check the secondary point about `I1` beyond confirming it is a hypothesis of `exclusive_bytes` and is not named in point 3.\",\"evidence\":\"1. `grep -n DDSound formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` finds only l.91 (\\\"valent sur tout état atteint sous `DDSound k`\\\", in (b)) and l.247 (\\\"6. **`DDSound` réel, adresses épinglées, concurrence.** Hors périmètre de la passe.\\\"). Nothing in Résultats principaux 3 (l.27-32) mentions it. That point reads: \\\"Les hypothèses MM-03 (`WF3`, `NoDangling`, `FpLeaves`, `FrameOwnedLive`) sont prouvées sur les états atteints. Les autres restent des obligations ouvertes, voir (d) 4 : `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat` ; `MM02.WF`, `dec` et `stat` ; l'hypothèse « une racine »…\\\". (d) 4 (l.240-244) lists FreeSound, PlacementOK, NewLayout, TokCompat, MM02.WF, dec, stat, with no DDSound.\\n2. Module signatures:\\n- formal/Ern/MM03.lean:8381 `theorem reachable_invariants {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) ...`\\n- formal/Ern/MM23.lean:1233 `theorem reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) ...`, whose docstring says \\\"under `DDSound k`, the hypothesis under which `WF3` is proved on reached states\\\"\\n- MM23.lean:1268, 1281, 1292: `r1_read3_reachable`, `r2_write3_reachable` and `r2_writeShared_reachable` each take `(hdd : DDSound k)`\\n- MM23.lean:1766 `r6_exit_reachable ... (hdd : DDSound k)`\\n- MM23.lean:1778 `r4_no_dead_cover ... (hdd : DDSound k) (hr : Reachable k statics s3) (hR : Repr tok L s3 s2)`\\n- MM23.lean:1798-1799 `exclusive_bytes ... (hlw : LayoutWF L s3 s2) (hI1 : I1 s3)`\\n3. The spec qualifies reached-state results with DDSound. MM-03.3 l.185: \\\"Sur les états atteints depuis `S3.init statics` sous `DDSound(K)`\\\". l.553: \\\"sur tous les états atteints depuis `S3.init statics`, **sous `DDSound(K)`**\\\". l.521: \\\"La réalisation de `DDSound` à partir de dispositions mémoire réelles fait partie du raffinement de MM-03 vers MM-02\\\". l.614: \\\"Sans `DDSound`, le témoin `split_unsound_without_DD` réfute l'exclusivité globale\\\".\\n4. The brief (task_mm23_p1.md l.37) puts \\\"`DDSound` réel depuis `LayoutWF` et `DeclaredDisjoint`\\\" out of scope. It therefore remains an open hypothesis that point 3's list should name, not something proved.\"}},{\"lens\":\"report\",\"id\":\"F3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, (b) preamble\",\"claim\":\"The rewritten per-theorem list of MM-02 hypotheses is incomplete, and its closing line is false. `PlacementOK` is also a hypothesis of `repr_init`. The `MM02.Pow2` alignment hypotheses are not mentioned. 'les autres théorèmes n'ont pas d'hypothèse MM-02' is false for `r6_free`, whose `FreeSound` is a predicate on the MM-02 state `s2`.\",\"evidence\":\"Preamble: '`MM02.WF s2` et `PlacementOK` : hypothèses de `r6_alloc` et `r6_enter` ; les autres théorèmes n'ont pas d'hypothèse MM-02.' Module: repr_init has `(hpl : PlacementOK pl)` and `(hg : ∀ i ∈ rootIdx …, 0 &lt; (g i).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (g i).align)` (MM23.lean:855-858). r6_alloc has `(hg : 0 &lt; (g i).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (g i).align)` (1517) and r6_enter has `hg … MM02.Pow2` (1597). r6_free has `(hfs : FreeSound k C L s3 s2 p auth)`, where `FreeSound … := … AllocP s2 (L l).alloc fun a =&gt; ∃ d, a.freeAuth = some d ∧ C auth d` (1472-1475). The report itself, (c) 13, says FreeSound 'est posée dans l'état MM-02 courant', and (e) 4 says '`FreeSound` est posée sur l'état MM-02'.\",\"fix\":\"Add `repr_init` to the PlacementOK line. Mention the alignment hypotheses (`MM02.Pow2`) of r6_alloc, r6_enter and repr_init. Either say that r6_free's `FreeSound` reads `s2` (and r6_exit's `TokCompat` reads MM-02's `Compatible`), or drop 'les autres théorèmes n'ont pas d'hypothèse MM-02'.\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"Confirmed, minor. In the (b) preamble that commit 332a8b3 rewrote, `PlacementOK` is listed as an MM-02 hypothesis of `r6_alloc` and `r6_enter` only, but `repr_init` takes it too. The closing line puts `r6_free` among the theorems with no MM-02 hypothesis, yet its `FreeSound` hypothesis is stated on the MM-02 state `s2` and on MM-02's `Compatible` (`C`). The report itself says in (e) 4 that FreeSound \\\"est posée sur l'état MM-02\\\". The report is also inconsistent: (d) 4 counts only `MM02.WF`, `dec` and `stat` as MM-02, while the (b) preamble also counts `PlacementOK`. Under the preamble's own grouping, the list is incomplete and its closing sentence is false. Two things limit the impact. The repr_init bullet later in (b) does list `PlacementOK` and the alignment hypotheses, and the R6 table lists the alignment hypotheses (stated with `MM02.Pow2`) and `FreeSound`. Whether the `Pow2` alignment hypotheses count as MM-02 is a matter of grouping. The `repr_init`/`PlacementOK` omission is a plain error.\",\"evidence\":\"Report formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:85-88: \\\"Les hypothèses MM-02 dépendent du théorème : ... - `MM02.WF s2` et `PlacementOK` : hypothèses de `r6_alloc` et `r6_enter` ; - les autres théorèmes n'ont pas d'hypothèse MM-02.\\\" (added by 332a8b3, per `git show 332a8b3`).\\n\\nLean check: `lake env lean` on the scratch file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/verif2/f3.lean.\\n- `#check @repr_init` shows \\\"∀ {pl : Placement}, PlacementOK pl → ∀ {g}, (∀ i, i ∈ rootIdx … → 0 &lt; (g i).align ∧ Ern.MM02.Pow2 (g i).align) → …\\\", which is MM23.lean:857-858.\\n- `#check @r6_free` shows \\\"WF3 s3 → Repr tok L s3 s2 → FreeSound k C L s3 s2 p auth → FreeStep … → …\\\".\\n- `#print FreeSound` shows \\\"k.Deallocable p → k.FreeCompat p auth → ∀ l ∈ footprint s3.P p, AllocP s2 (L l).alloc fun a =&gt; ∃ d, a.freeAuth = some d ∧ C auth d\\\". The hypothesis reads the MM-02 state `s2\n... (truncated 8133 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdhczph0j.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_675af73d-f92/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/mm23-second-check-wf_675af73d-f92.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_675af73d-f92'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>7</agent_count><agents_done>7</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>724396</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>86</tool_uses><duration_ms>537176</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
