{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","id":"88f21b8a-58b4-4938-8b6e-f2e3af1d3f83","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:29:02.404Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"d1aa6c2254c890b11835611a868b353c28b0e75545aafd34fb8d8155d691dfb1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"b5030411-f1f4-466a-a728-e3d1cdc8151b","keep":343,"tail":["c14336dfef37360df54f673e06ae7a2652aa66cfec84bcad72f009008c06d64f","c5727269330847c7e9fd384861747cc1633301cdfc0d454716c4e862ae7bb4fb"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",344,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0460e6ff187ec99bbe77e77fc69e82505e83349d39cb6859dd7ea3189932fdda"}
{"parentUuid":"f1a7bf30-80e9-435d-a385-7e10e1a96242","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgawsUgHxQsZu1FS8auKq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Jalon 2, passe 1 is done. The new module `formal/Ern/MM23.lean` and the French report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` are committed on `formal/refinement_0.1`. R1, R2, R4, R6 and `exclusive_bytes` are proved, under hypotheses that the report lists in full.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `lake build` passes with no warnings, and there is no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide` or `noncomputable`.\n- 97 theorems and 73 examples. A Lean script checks all 153 theorem constants of the module: none uses an axiom other than `propext` and `Quot.sound`.\n- `MM02.lean` and `MM03.lean` are unchanged.\n\n**What is proved:**\n- **`Repr`:** the relation between the two models (K1–K3) can be checked by `decide`. A negative test for each of its clauses shows each one rejects a wrong MM-02 state.\n- **`repr_init`:** the initial state is in `Repr` with the MM-02 state built from the static allocations and writes.\n- **R1, R2:** an `ok` read or write in MM-03 gives `ok` MM-02 steps (never `ub`), the read returns the bytes of the range, and `Repr` is preserved.\n- **R6:** proved for each operation in K4's scope.\n- **R4:** an active authority never covers a leaf whose allocation is dead.\n- **`exclusive_bytes`:** proved in a stronger form than the brief asks. The conditions \"b active\" and \"b not descending from a\" turn out to be unnecessary.\n- **Witnesses:** one scenario starting from `S3.init` runs every operation and applies each theorem to it, with the MM-02 sequence shown explicitly.\n\n**Limits you should know:**\n- **Draft gaps behind R1 and R2:** the draft MM-03 omits two clauses of its text, that leaves read or written are usable (O9.1–O11.1) and that footprints are made of leaves (WF3 §2.1.4). R1 and R2 therefore assume two invariants, which I proved on all reached states under `DDSound k`. A kept counterexample shows R1 fails without them.\n- **Still assumed, not established:** `DDSound`, `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, MM-02 `WF`, `dec` and `stat`.\n- **Not covered:** a theorem simulating an entire execution (`transfer`, `store` and `issue` are out of scope), and `alloc` of a shape with several roots, which the draft accepts.\n\n**For the arbiter, the main questions in (e):**\n- At `exitFrame`, is a local owned by another local an automatic allocation of the frame or owned storage? The module treats it as owned storage, so its allocation leaks if not freed.\n- When `free` or `exitFrame` kills storage owned by the dying root, its MM-02 allocation is required to stay live. K3 reads the other way; this follows K4's single deallocation step, but it is my choice.\n- Should `alloc` be restricted to one root, or map to one allocation step per root?\n- `Repr` no longer takes `k`, because no K3 clause reads K.\n\nThe report's section (f) lists six gaps between the drafts and their texts, each with a witness.\n\n**Review:** two independent reviewers found nothing blocking; their findings led to stronger statements, new witnesses and two new questions. A verification workflow then confirmed 10 report errors out of 15 findings, and a second check confirmed 4 out of 5; all are fixed.\n\n**ub-mode log** (full log of 18 entries at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/mm23/log.md`):\n- Each piece started with a `decide` test before the definitions, for example `Repr` on the initial state, true with the static's write and false without it.\n- I committed once per step, then once per review round.\n- Lean pitfalls found: `omega` on a conjunction goal pulls in `Classical.choice`, and `meta` is a keyword. I replaced the grep-based axiom sweep, which missed names inside the case namespaces, with a Lean script.\n- Nothing is pushed: the brief's « Pas de merge, pas de PR » overrides ub-mode's \"push to the main line\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":318,"cache_read_input_tokens":718078,"output_tokens":1485,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":318,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1485,"cache_read_input_tokens":718078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":318},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a2016d96-793f-4f9c-8bd6-b8b9e3d560a4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgawsUMh4jcG6q1GULJJn","requestRef":"88f21b8a-58b4-4938-8b6e-f2e3af1d3f83","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"38f1d6b2-8d61-4a4b-bece-72d300d6ac63","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:29:17.881Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
