{"parentUuid":"581b85e4-b6c4-42ae-b565-0f39ad406f03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4hf8dcFVDYCC7Rs3L6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm delegating two independent MM-03 facts (leaf correspondence under `SameShape` and the pinned-leaf usability invariant) to a workflow whose agents only import the unchanged `Ern.MM03`, keeping them safe from my upcoming `Repr` edits, while I proceed with step 1.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"output_tokens":9870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9870,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a9d3d584-21eb-4191-885e-362eea089700","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb4heoXwMeg7Jartp6Xo","requestRef":"5734a3ce-c514-4f3f-aafa-729c41cad4f0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"abeb64dc-6a0c-466f-8406-c6e7a6081c44","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:59:27.368Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"abeb64dc-6a0c-466f-8406-c6e7a6081c44","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4hf8dcFVDYCC7Rs3L6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0126gnUmdSGb6YERPuC7vxv6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; mkdir -p $SP/p2work && cat > $SP/task_mm23_p2.md <<'EOF'\n(brief of jalon 2 pass 2 — see conversation; arbitrages L1–L8 replace K where stated)\nL1 enterFrame locals owned directly by frame (owning element out of language: hypothesis or envelope); statics may be owned by statics; K.Deallocable false on statics.\nL2 alloc shape has exactly one root (hypothesis).\nL3 MM02.WF s2 is a clause of Repr; Repr does not take k; Moved/Uninit impose nothing on bytes.\nL4 token of alloc'd allocations = provider's; ghost provOf root ↦ provider; FreeCompat p auth instantiated by Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p)); prove freeSound_derived (replaces FreeSound): content = conservation along the trace of the token of each allocated root's MM-02 allocation (Repr imposes it).\nL5 free p ↦ one DeallocStep on p's allocation; owned storage keeps live allocation (leaked kept). Same at exitFrame.\nL6 transfer ↦ per corresponding leaf pair (iso order): ReadStep src range then WriteStep dst range with bytes read incl. provenance; hypothesis SameSizeAlong; held authorities/owned storage no step; src bytes stay init in MM-02. store a p ↦ WriteStep on p's range of ptrBytes; obligation decode (ptrBytes x) = address of first byte of region of x (base + off of first leaf) and each byte's provenance = allocation of that region. issue ↦ WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage); available/issued = abstract arena state (library obligation). reset ↦ no step.\nL7 ddSound_of_layout: under LayoutWF, instantiating K.DeclaredDisjoint by byte-range disjointness of the leaves of both regions satisfies DDSound; obligation classed \"bibliothèque\".\nL8 pinned_address_stable: for each ok MM-03 step and its MM-02 sequence, every leaf pinned (static or dynamic) before keeps a LIVE allocation and the same address (base + off) after; docstring: MM-02 models no physical move.\nSteps (one commit each): 1 L1–L5; 2 L6; 3 L7; 4 L8; 5 simulation (any Reachable execution from S3.init statics, L/placement/tokens/ptrBytes fixed once, exists MM-02 execution from repr_init's initial state, all ok, in Repr at each step; remaining hypotheses in the statement); 6 cases (one per new op + full execution: alloc, arena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free, exit).\nOut of scope: concurrency, finite addresses (spec 11), arena metadata representation, low-level translation, fixes to MM-03 draft.\nRules: zero sorry; axioms ⊆ {propext, Quot.sound} for all module constants; no noncomputable; build w/o warnings; docstrings cite clause/arbitrage; nothing invented; no weakened statement; adversarial review on L4 (circularity), L6 (provenance/address lost or fabricated), L7, simulation (per-step parameters making it vacuous); counterexamples kept.\nDeliverable: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md: (a) clause→decl; (b) status R1,R2,R4,R6 (full scope), ddSound_of_layout, pinned_address_stable, freeSound_derived, simulation; (c) decisions; (d) unproven; (e) questions; (f) final list of simulation hypotheses classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save the pass-2 brief summary to the scratchpad"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"output_tokens":9870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9870,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0126gnUmdSGb6YERPuC7vxv6":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; mkdir -p $SP/p2work && cat > $SP/task_mm23_p2.md <<'EOF'\n(brief of jalon 2 pass 2 — see conversation; arbitrages L1–L8 replace K where stated)\nL1 enterFrame locals owned directly by frame (owning element out of language: hypothesis or envelope); statics may be owned by statics; K.Deallocable false on statics.\nL2 alloc shape has exactly one root (hypothesis).\nL3 MM02.WF s2 is a clause of Repr; Repr does not take k; Moved/Uninit impose nothing on bytes.\nL4 token of alloc'd allocations = provider's; ghost provOf root ↦ provider; FreeCompat p auth instantiated by Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p)); prove freeSound_derived (replaces FreeSound): content = conservation along the trace of the token of each allocated root's MM-02 allocation (Repr imposes it).\nL5 free p ↦ one DeallocStep on p's allocation; owned storage keeps live allocation (leaked kept). Same at exitFrame.\nL6 transfer ↦ per corresponding leaf pair (iso order): ReadStep src range then WriteStep dst range with bytes read incl. provenance; hypothesis SameSizeAlong; held authorities/owned storage no step; src bytes stay init in MM-02. store a p ↦ WriteStep on p's range of ptrBytes; obligation decode (ptrBytes x) = address of first byte of region of x (base + off of first leaf) and each byte's provenance = allocation of that region. issue ↦ WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage); available/issued = abstract arena state (library obligation). reset ↦ no step.\nL7 ddSound_of_layout: under LayoutWF, instantiating K.DeclaredDisjoint by byte-range disjointness of the leaves of both regions satisfies DDSound; obligation classed \"bibliothèque\".\nL8 pinned_address_stable: for each ok MM-03 step and its MM-02 sequence, every leaf pinned (static or dynamic) before keeps a LIVE allocation and the same address (base + off) after; docstring: MM-02 models no physical move.\nSteps (one commit each): 1 L1–L5; 2 L6; 3 L7; 4 L8; 5 simulation (any Reachable execution from S3.init statics, L/placement/tokens/ptrBytes fixed once, exists MM-02 execution from repr_init's initial state, all ok, in Repr at each step; remaining hypotheses in the statement); 6 cases (one per new op + full execution: alloc, arena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free, exit).\nOut of scope: concurrency, finite addresses (spec 11), arena metadata representation, low-level translation, fixes to MM-03 draft.\nRules: zero sorry; axioms ⊆ {propext, Quot.sound} for all module constants; no noncomputable; build w/o warnings; docstrings cite clause/arbitrage; nothing invented; no weakened statement; adversarial review on L4 (circularity), L6 (provenance/address lost or fabricated), L7, simulation (per-step parameters making it vacuous); counterexamples kept.\nDeliverable: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md: (a) clause→decl; (b) status R1,R2,R4,R6 (full scope), ddSound_of_layout, pinned_address_stable, freeSound_derived, simulation; (c) decisions; (d) unproven; (e) questions; (f) final list of simulation hypotheses classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save the pass-2 brief summary to the scratchpad"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a9d3d584-21eb-4191-885e-362eea089700","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb4heoXwMeg7Jartp6Xo","requestRef":"5734a3ce-c514-4f3f-aafa-729c41cad4f0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25af63a3-2b8f-4be3-b055-3c567f25c749","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:59:37.897Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"25af63a3-2b8f-4be3-b055-3c567f25c749","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4hf8dcFVDYCC7Rs3L6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W3pdB4VuzVdimrRifEHGQE","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'mm23-p2-lemmas',\n  description: 'Prove two independent MM-03 lemma families for MM23 pass 2 in scratch files, then verify each',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Prove', detail: 'transfer correspondence; pinned leaves stay usable' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'independent compile, axiom and statement check' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work'\nconst RULES = `Environment: Lean 4 core v4.35, NO Mathlib (tactics like set, tauto, linarith, aesop do not exist). Work ONLY in a new scratch file under ${SP}/ (name given below). Never modify any file in the repository /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern and NEVER run \"lake build\" (other work is editing the repository concurrently). Check your file with: cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean ${SP}/<file> . The file must start with \"import Ern.MM03\" then \"open Ern.MM03\" then \"namespace Ern.MM23\" ... \"end Ern.MM23\". Do not import Ern.MM23. lake is not on PATH; there is no \"timeout\" command.\nRules (strict): no sorry, admit, native_decide, axiom declarations, noncomputable; every theorem must depend only on propext and Quot.sound — check with \"#print axioms <name>\" at the end of the file, then remove those #print lines from the final file. Known pitfalls: omega proving a CONJUNCTION goal pulls Classical.choice (split the goal first); by_cases on a Prop without Decidable instance pulls Classical; lemmas like List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem, List.nodup_range, List.getElem?_mapIdx pull Classical. \"meta\" is a keyword (never name a hypothesis meta). if_pos/if_neg are deprecated (use simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]). No warnings allowed (unused variables, unused simp args, deprecations).\nRead formal/Ern/MM03.lean for definitions and existing lemmas (grep for names; key ones: footprint, mem_footprint, partOf, isLeaf, parentOf, chain, chain_cons, chain_lt, kids, mem_kids, kids_nil_iff, posIn, corr, corrF, corr_src, corr_step, corr_partOf, SameShape, WF3 and its projections WF3.parts/parent_lt/ownerOf/deadOf, exists_rootPlace, footprint_sub, S3.Usable, Usable.mono, Usable.congr, usable_of_part, usable_of_partOf, Step, KStep, Reachable, reachable_invariants, step relations and effects: enterEff, enter_usable_old/new/back, allocEff, alloc_usable_old/new/back, transferEff, transfer_usable_fwd/back, endUseS/endUseEff, EndUsePre, EndingLeaf, freeS/freeEff, FreePre, FreedLeaf, exitEff, exitEff_eq, ExitPre, pinEff, PinPre, UnpinPre, shapeP lemmas shape_footprint_old etc.). Docstrings in English citing the MM-03.3 rule. Keep proofs readable.\nFinal answer: the absolute path of the file, the exact statements proved, and the output of the final check command (must be empty).`\n\nconst TASKS = [\n  { key: 'corr', file: 'corr_leaves.lean', prompt: `${RULES}\nFile: corr_leaves.lean. Goal: the leaves of the source and destination of a transfer correspond under SameShape (MM-03.3 O4.2, J1 ordered isomorphism). Prove exactly these (you may add helper lemmas):\ntheorem corr_leaf_fwd {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hd : dst < s.P.length) (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst) {l : Nat} (hl : l ∈ footprint s.P src) : ∃ l', corr s.P src dst l = some l' ∧ l' ∈ footprint s.P dst\ntheorem corr_leaf_back {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst) {l' : Nat} (hl' : l' ∈ footprint s.P dst) : ∃ l ∈ footprint s.P src, corr s.P src dst l = some l'\ntheorem corr_inj {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hs : src < s.P.length) (hd : dst < s.P.length) (hno : ¬ overlap s.P src dst) {r₁ r₂ x : Nat} (h₁ : partOf s.P r₁ src) (h₂ : partOf s.P r₂ src) (e₁ : corr s.P src dst r₁ = some x) (e₂ : corr s.P src dst r₂ = some x) : r₁ = r₂\nIf corr_inj turns out to need an additional hypothesis that is true under TransferPre (for example SameShape), you may add it, but say so explicitly. If corr_inj is false under these hypotheses, give a concrete counterexample checked by decide instead of a proof.` },\n  { key: 'pinned', file: 'pinned_live.lean', prompt: `${RULES}\nFile: pinned_live.lean. Goal: on reached states, a pinned leaf (dynamically, s.pin l = true, or statically, k.Pinned l) of an existing place is usable, and stays usable across any ok step (MM-03.3 O15: transfer, endUse, free, exitFrame are rejected on pinned leaves; O12 C5, O13 B6, O7 B4, O4.5). Define and prove exactly:\ndef PinnedLive (k : K) (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ l < s.P.length, isLeaf s.P l → (s.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) → s.Usable l\ntheorem step_pinned_usable {k : K} {s s' : S3} (hw : WF3 s) (hp : PinnedLive k s) (h : Step k s s') : ∀ l < s.P.length, isLeaf s.P l → (s.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) → s'.Usable l\ntheorem step_pinnedLive {k : K} {s s' : S3} (hw : WF3 s) (hp : PinnedLive k s) (h : Step k s s') : PinnedLive k s'\ntheorem reachable_pinnedLive {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {s : S3} (h : Reachable k statics s) : PinnedLive k s\n(Step is MM03's union of KStep, newArena, issue, reset; Reachable's constructors map to Step constructors; reachable_invariants gives WF3 under DDSound.) Hints: endUseEff = cleanup (endUseS s p) and cleanup changes only A, so usability after endUse is usability in endUseS; EndUsePre's last clause forbids pinned EndingLeaf; same for free with FreedLeaf; ExitPre's pin clause covers places usable before and not after (a leaf is in its own footprint); transfer keeps usability (transfer_usable_fwd/back with TransferPre); enter/alloc keep old usability and new places are usable; pin marks leaves of a usable place (a leaf of a usable place is usable: usable_of_partOf); new places have pin = false. If any statement is false, give a decide-checked counterexample from a reached state instead.` },\n]\n\nphase('Prove')\nconst out = await pipeline(\n  TASKS,\n  t => agent(t.prompt, { label: `prove:${t.key}`, phase: 'Prove' }),\n  (res, t) => agent(`${RULES}\nYou are an independent verifier (do not rewrite the proofs). A prover claims to have written ${SP}/${t.file} for this goal:\n---\n${t.prompt}\n---\nProver's report:\n${res}\nCheck: (1) the file compiles with no output using the check command (no errors, no warnings); (2) append temporary \"#print axioms\" for every theorem into a COPY of the file (${SP}/check_${t.file}) and confirm only propext and Quot.sound appear; (3) the statements in the file match the required statements exactly (no added hypothesis, no weakened conclusion) unless the prover declared and justified an addition; (4) no sorry/admit/native_decide/axiom/noncomputable. Answer with a verdict line \"VERIFIED\" or \"REJECTED\", then the evidence (command outputs).`, { label: `verify:${t.key}`, phase: 'Verify' }).then(v => ({ key: t.key, file: `${SP}/${t.file}`, prover: res, verifier: v }))\n)\nreturn out\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"output_tokens":9870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9870,"cache_read_input_tokens":766426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1622},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W3pdB4VuzVdimrRifEHGQE":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'mm23-p2-lemmas',\n  description: 'Prove two independent MM-03 lemma families for MM23 pass 2 in scratch files, then verify each',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Prove', detail: 'transfer correspondence; pinned leaves stay usable' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'independent compile, axiom and statement check' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work'\nconst RULES = `Environment: Lean 4 core v4.35, NO Mathlib (tactics like set, tauto, linarith, aesop do not exist). Work ONLY in a new scratch file under ${SP}/ (name given below). Never modify any file in the repository /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern and NEVER run \"lake build\" (other work is editing the repository concurrently). Check your file with: cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean ${SP}/<file> . The file must start with \"import Ern.MM03\" then \"open Ern.MM03\" then \"namespace Ern.MM23\" ... \"end Ern.MM23\". Do not import Ern.MM23. lake is not on PATH; there is no \"timeout\" command.\nRules (strict): no sorry, admit, native_decide, axiom declarations, noncomputable; every theorem must depend only on propext and Quot.sound — check with \"#print axioms <name>\" at the end of the file, then remove those #print lines from the final file. Known pitfalls: omega proving a CONJUNCTION goal pulls Classical.choice (split the goal first); by_cases on a Prop without Decidable instance pulls Classical; lemmas like List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem, List.nodup_range, List.getElem?_mapIdx pull Classical. \"meta\" is a keyword (never name a hypothesis meta). if_pos/if_neg are deprecated (use simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]). No warnings allowed (unused variables, unused simp args, deprecations).\nRead formal/Ern/MM03.lean for definitions and existing lemmas (grep for names; key ones: footprint, mem_footprint, partOf, isLeaf, parentOf, chain, chain_cons, chain_lt, kids, mem_kids, kids_nil_iff, posIn, corr, corrF, corr_src, corr_step, corr_partOf, SameShape, WF3 and its projections WF3.parts/parent_lt/ownerOf/deadOf, exists_rootPlace, footprint_sub, S3.Usable, Usable.mono, Usable.congr, usable_of_part, usable_of_partOf, Step, KStep, Reachable, reachable_invariants, step relations and effects: enterEff, enter_usable_old/new/back, allocEff, alloc_usable_old/new/back, transferEff, transfer_usable_fwd/back, endUseS/endUseEff, EndUsePre, EndingLeaf, freeS/freeEff, FreePre, FreedLeaf, exitEff, exitEff_eq, ExitPre, pinEff, PinPre, UnpinPre, shapeP lemmas shape_footprint_old etc.). Docstrings in English citing the MM-03.3 rule. Keep proofs readable.\nFinal answer: the absolute path of the file, the exact statements proved, and the output of the final check command (must be empty).`\n\nconst TASKS = [\n  { key: 'corr', file: 'corr_leaves.lean', prompt: `${RULES}\nFile: corr_leaves.lean. Goal: the leaves of the source and destination of a transfer correspond under SameShape (MM-03.3 O4.2, J1 ordered isomorphism). Prove exactly these (you may add helper lemmas):\ntheorem corr_leaf_fwd {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hd : dst < s.P.length) (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst) {l : Nat} (hl : l ∈ footprint s.P src) : ∃ l', corr s.P src dst l = some l' ∧ l' ∈ footprint s.P dst\ntheorem corr_leaf_back {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst) {l' : Nat} (hl' : l' ∈ footprint s.P dst) : ∃ l ∈ footprint s.P src, corr s.P src dst l = some l'\ntheorem corr_inj {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hs : src < s.P.length) (hd : dst < s.P.length) (hno : ¬ overlap s.P src dst) {r₁ r₂ x : Nat} (h₁ : partOf s.P r₁ src) (h₂ : partOf s.P r₂ src) (e₁ : corr s.P src dst r₁ = some x) (e₂ : corr s.P src dst r₂ = some x) : r₁ = r₂\nIf corr_inj turns out to need an additional hypothesis that is true under TransferPre (for example SameShape), you may add it, but say so explicitly. If corr_inj is false under these hypotheses, give a concrete counterexample checked by decide instead of a proof.` },\n  { key: 'pinned', file: 'pinned_live.lean', prompt: `${RULES}\nFile: pinned_live.lean. Goal: on reached states, a pinned leaf (dynamically, s.pin l = true, or statically, k.Pinned l) of an existing place is usable, and stays usable across any ok step (MM-03.3 O15: transfer, endUse, free, exitFrame are rejected on pinned leaves; O12 C5, O13 B6, O7 B4, O4.5). Define and prove exactly:\ndef PinnedLive (k : K) (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ l < s.P.length, isLeaf s.P l → (s.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) → s.Usable l\ntheorem step_pinned_usable {k : K} {s s' : S3} (hw : WF3 s) (hp : PinnedLive k s) (h : Step k s s') : ∀ l < s.P.length, isLeaf s.P l → (s.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) → s'.Usable l\ntheorem step_pinnedLive {k : K} {s s' : S3} (hw : WF3 s) (hp : PinnedLive k s) (h : Step k s s') : PinnedLive k s'\ntheorem reachable_pinnedLive {k : K} (hdd : DDSound k) {statics : Statics} {s : S3} (h : Reachable k statics s) : PinnedLive k s\n(Step is MM03's union of KStep, newArena, issue, reset; Reachable's constructors map to Step constructors; reachable_invariants gives WF3 under DDSound.) Hints: endUseEff = cleanup (endUseS s p) and cleanup changes only A, so usability after endUse is usability in endUseS; EndUsePre's last clause forbids pinned EndingLeaf; same for free with FreedLeaf; ExitPre's pin clause covers places usable before and not after (a leaf is in its own footprint); transfer keeps usability (transfer_usable_fwd/back with TransferPre); enter/alloc keep old usability and new places are usable; pin marks leaves of a usable place (a leaf of a usable place is usable: usable_of_partOf); new places have pin = false. If any statement is false, give a decide-checked counterexample from a reached state instead.` },\n]\n\nphase('Prove')\nconst out = await pipeline(\n  TASKS,\n  t => agent(t.prompt, { label: `prove:${t.key}`, phase: 'Prove' }),\n  (res, t) => agent(`${RULES}\nYou are an independent verifier (do not rewrite the proofs). A prover claims to have written ${SP}/${t.file} for this goal:\n---\n${t.prompt}\n---\nProver's report:\n${res}\nCheck: (1) the file compiles with no output using the check command (no errors, no warnings); (2) append temporary \"#print axioms\" for every theorem into a COPY of the file (${SP}/check_${t.file}) and confirm only propext and Quot.sound appear; (3) the statements in the file match the required statements exactly (no added hypothesis, no weakened conclusion) unless the prover declared and justified an addition; (4) no sorry/admit/native_decide/axiom/noncomputable. Answer with a verdict line \"VERIFIED\" or \"REJECTED\", then the evidence (command outputs).`, { label: `verify:${t.key}`, phase: 'Verify' }).then(v => ({ key: t.key, file: `${SP}/${t.file}`, prover: res, verifier: v }))\n)\nreturn out\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a9d3d584-21eb-4191-885e-362eea089700","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgb4heoXwMeg7Jartp6Xo","requestRef":"5734a3ce-c514-4f3f-aafa-729c41cad4f0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b4cb814-192c-4365-a3c6-fd93173efb8b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:00:04.380Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
