14Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"3ee7305f-34f5-4c72-aaba-ad9f9751dfbc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"afea6d65-2af9-420c-969b-b55d07c96f18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAAfN7iGvPo5TYU8WwYZ7q","type":"tool_result","content":"3:Each verdict is checked by `decide` on the precondition of the MM-03 step and on `Repr`, which is\n24:/-- `repr_init` on the static storage, and the same verdict by `decide`; without the write of the\n25:static, `Repr` fails (K3: an `Init` leaf has its bytes initialised). -/\n26:example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 :=\n27:  (repr_init (C := fun _ _ => False) (ObR := obR) (ObW := obW) (by decide) topPlacement_ok\n29:example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 := by decide\n30:example : ¬ Repr tk L (S3.init st)\n36:root authority stays active, `read3` is `ok`, `Repr` holds, and the MM-02 read is `ub`: R1 needs\n40:example : Repr tk L cx cx2 := by decide\n166:/-- `Repr` at each point, by `decide`. -/\n167:example : Repr tk L e0 m0 ∧ Repr tk L e1 m1 ∧ Repr tk L e2 m2 ∧ Repr tk L e3 m3 ∧\n168:    Repr tk L e6 m3 ∧ Repr tk L e8 m8 ∧ Repr tk L e12 m12 ∧ Repr tk L e15 m12 ∧\n169:    Repr tk L e16 m16 ∧ Repr tk L f13 mF := by decide\n171:/-- K3: initial state (`repr_init`). -/\n172:example : AllOk C obR obW MM02.State.empty (initOps topPlacement g tk L w st) ∧ Repr tk L e0 m0 :=\n173:  repr_init (by decide) topPlacement_ok (by decide) (by decide) (fun _ _ _ => trivial) (by decide)\n175:example : AllOk C obR obW m0 ops1 ∧ Repr tk L e1 m1 :=\n176:  r6_enter (reachable_invariants kc_dd r0).1 (by decide) (wf2 _) topPlacement_ok (by decide)\n179:example : AllOk C obR obW m1 ops2 ∧ Repr tk L e2 m2 :=\n180:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r1 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 1 [1] e1 (.ok e2))\n182:example : AllOk C obR obW m2 ops3 ∧ Repr tk L e3 m3 :=\n183:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r2 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 2 [2] e2 (.ok e3))\n185:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 ops7 ∧ Repr tk L e7 m7 :=\n186:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r6 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 5 [4] e6 (.ok e7))\n189:example : AllOk C obR obW m7 ops8 ∧ Repr tk L e8 m8 :=\n190:  r2_writeShared_reachable kc_dd r7 (by decide)\n193:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 (readOps m3 L [1]) ∧ Repr tk L e3 (exec m3 (readOps m3 L [1])) :=\n194:  r6_read3 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).1 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).2.1.nd\n204:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 ops12 ∧ Repr tk L e12 m12 :=\n205:  r6_alloc (i := 0) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r11).1 (by decide) wfm8 topPlacement_ok\n209:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e12 (exec m12 []) :=\n210:  r6_alloc_fail (by decide)\n213:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 opsF ∧ Repr tk L f13 mF := by\n214:  refine r6_free (k := KC) (auth := 7) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r12).1 (by decide) ?_\n223:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 ops16 ∧ Repr tk L e16 m16 :=\n224:  r6_exit_reachable kc_dd r15 (by decide) (fun _ => rfl) (.ok (by decide))\n229:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e4 (exec m3 []) :=\n230:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.derive (.ok (by decide) : DeriveStep 3 4 .observe e3 (.ok e4)))\n231:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e5 (exec m3 []) :=\n232:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.release (.ok (by decide) : ReleaseStep 4 e4 (.ok e5)))\n233:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e6 (exec m3 []) :=\n234:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.split (.ok (by decide) : SplitStep KC 3 [[4], [5]] e5 (.ok e6)))\n235:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e9 (exec m8 []) :=\n236:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.depend (.ok (by decide) : DependStep 2 1 e8 (.ok e9)))\n237:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e10 (exec m8 []) :=\n238:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.pin (.ok (by decide) : PinStep 2 e9 (.ok e10)))\n239:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e11 (exec m8 []) :=\n240:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.unpin (.ok (by decide) : UnpinStep KC 2 e10 (.ok e11)))\n241:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e13 (exec m12 []) :=\n242:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.newArena (.ok (by decide) : NewArenaStep 6 7 e12 (.ok e13)))\n243:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e14 (exec m12 []) :=\n244:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.reset (.ok (by decide) : ResetAtStep KC 0 2 e13 (.ok e14)))\n245:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e15 (exec m12 []) :=\n246:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.endUse (.ok (by decide) : EndUseStep KC 2 e14 (.ok e15)))\n253:  (r4_no_dead_cover (tok := tk) kc_dd r16 (by decide) 0 _ rfl rfl 0 (List.mem_singleton_self _)).2.2\n255:/-- `exclusive_bytes`: after `split`, authority 5 has effective `Modify` on leaf 4; the root 3,\n261:  exclusive_bytes (L := L) (s2 := m3) (by decide) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r6).2.1.base.1\n270:example : Repr tk L0 e12 m12z := by decide\n272:/-- Each clause of `Repr` rejects a wrong MM-02 state: a usable root with a dead allocation; a\n275:example : ¬ Repr tk L e3 (m3.dealloc 1) := by decide\n276:example : ¬ Repr tk L e15 (m12.dealloc 4) := by decide\n278:example : LayoutWF Lsh e1 m1 ∧ ¬ Repr tk Lsh e1 m1 := by decide\n279:example : ¬ Repr (fun f => 200 + f) L e1 m1 := by decide\n280:example : ¬ Repr tk L e16 m12 ∧ ¬ Repr tk L f13 m12 := by decide\n284:fresh allocation satisfies `LayoutWF` but not `Repr` (two roots, one allocation). -/\n290:example : LayoutWF L2 e12b m12b ∧ ¬ Repr tk L2 e12b m12b := by decide\n294:allocation 5 of 7 stays live; deallocating it too breaks `Repr` (clause `leaked`). -/\n303:example : Repr tk La ao13 na13 ∧ Repr tk La af14 na14 := by decide\n305:example : ¬ Repr tk La af14 (na14.dealloc 5) := by decide\n335:  r1_read3 (tok := tk) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).1 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).2.1.nd\n347:6 stays live, as the clause `leaked` asks; deallocating it too breaks `Repr` (report, (c) 4). -/\n350:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 (exitOps L tk e12) ∧ Repr tk L eX (exec m12 (exitOps L tk e12)) :=\n351:  r6_exit_reachable kc_dd r12 (by decide) (fun _ => rfl) (.ok (by decide))\n354:example : ¬ Repr tk L eX ((exec m12 (exitOps L tk e12)).dealloc 4) := by decide\n385:example : Repr tk L o1 n1 ∧ Repr tk L o2 n2 := by decide\n387:example : Repr tk L o3 (exec n2 (exitOps L tk o2)) ∧ Repr tk L o3' (exec n1 (exitOps L tk o1)) := by\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6952e238-5007-4d86-a4e1-a190f1cec4c9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:05:14.433Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3:Each verdict is checked by `decide` on the precondition of the MM-03 step and on `Repr`, which is\n24:/-- `repr_init` on the static storage, and the same verdict by `decide`; without the write of the\n25:static, `Repr` fails (K3: an `Init` leaf has its bytes initialised). -/\n26:example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 :=\n27:  (repr_init (C := fun _ _ => False) (ObR := obR) (ObW := obW) (by decide) topPlacement_ok\n29:example : Repr tk L (S3.init st) s2 := by decide\n30:example : ¬ Repr tk L (S3.init st)\n36:root authority stays active, `read3` is `ok`, `Repr` holds, and the MM-02 read is `ub`: R1 needs\n40:example : Repr tk L cx cx2 := by decide\n166:/-- `Repr` at each point, by `decide`. -/\n167:example : Repr tk L e0 m0 ∧ Repr tk L e1 m1 ∧ Repr tk L e2 m2 ∧ Repr tk L e3 m3 ∧\n168:    Repr tk L e6 m3 ∧ Repr tk L e8 m8 ∧ Repr tk L e12 m12 ∧ Repr tk L e15 m12 ∧\n169:    Repr tk L e16 m16 ∧ Repr tk L f13 mF := by decide\n171:/-- K3: initial state (`repr_init`). -/\n172:example : AllOk C obR obW MM02.State.empty (initOps topPlacement g tk L w st) ∧ Repr tk L e0 m0 :=\n173:  repr_init (by decide) topPlacement_ok (by decide) (by decide) (fun _ _ _ => trivial) (by decide)\n175:example : AllOk C obR obW m0 ops1 ∧ Repr tk L e1 m1 :=\n176:  r6_enter (reachable_invariants kc_dd r0).1 (by decide) (wf2 _) topPlacement_ok (by decide)\n179:example : AllOk C obR obW m1 ops2 ∧ Repr tk L e2 m2 :=\n180:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r1 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 1 [1] e1 (.ok e2))\n182:example : AllOk C obR obW m2 ops3 ∧ Repr tk L e3 m3 :=\n183:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r2 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 2 [2] e2 (.ok e3))\n185:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 ops7 ∧ Repr tk L e7 m7 :=\n186:  r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r6 (by decide) (.ok (by decide) : Write3Step 5 [4] e6 (.ok e7))\n189:example : AllOk C obR obW m7 ops8 ∧ Repr tk L e8 m8 :=\n190:  r2_writeShared_reachable kc_dd r7 (by decide)\n193:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 (readOps m3 L [1]) ∧ Repr tk L e3 (exec m3 (readOps m3 L [1])) :=\n194:  r6_read3 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).1 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).2.1.nd\n204:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 ops12 ∧ Repr tk L e12 m12 :=\n205:  r6_alloc (i := 0) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r11).1 (by decide) wfm8 topPlacement_ok\n209:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e12 (exec m12 []) :=\n210:  r6_alloc_fail (by decide)\n213:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 opsF ∧ Repr tk L f13 mF := by\n214:  refine r6_free (k := KC) (auth := 7) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r12).1 (by decide) ?_\n223:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 ops16 ∧ Repr tk L e16 m16 :=\n224:  r6_exit_reachable kc_dd r15 (by decide) (fun _ => rfl) (.ok (by decide))\n229:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e4 (exec m3 []) :=\n230:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.derive (.ok (by decide) : DeriveStep 3 4 .observe e3 (.ok e4)))\n231:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e5 (exec m3 []) :=\n232:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.release (.ok (by decide) : ReleaseStep 4 e4 (.ok e5)))\n233:example : AllOk C obR obW m3 [] ∧ Repr tk L e6 (exec m3 []) :=\n234:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.split (.ok (by decide) : SplitStep KC 3 [[4], [5]] e5 (.ok e6)))\n235:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e9 (exec m8 []) :=\n236:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.depend (.ok (by decide) : DependStep 2 1 e8 (.ok e9)))\n237:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e10 (exec m8 []) :=\n238:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.pin (.ok (by decide) : PinStep 2 e9 (.ok e10)))\n239:example : AllOk C obR obW m8 [] ∧ Repr tk L e11 (exec m8 []) :=\n240:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.unpin (.ok (by decide) : UnpinStep KC 2 e10 (.ok e11)))\n241:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e13 (exec m12 []) :=\n242:  r6_noStep (k := KC) (by decide) (.newArena (.ok (by decide) : NewArenaStep 6 7 e12 (.ok e13)))\n243:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e14 (exec m12 []) :=\n244:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.reset (.ok (by decide) : ResetAtStep KC 0 2 e13 (.ok e14)))\n245:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 [] ∧ Repr tk L e15 (exec m12 []) :=\n246:  r6_noStep (by decide) (.endUse (.ok (by decide) : EndUseStep KC 2 e14 (.ok e15)))\n253:  (r4_no_dead_cover (tok := tk) kc_dd r16 (by decide) 0 _ rfl rfl 0 (List.mem_singleton_self _)).2.2\n255:/-- `exclusive_bytes`: after `split`, authority 5 has effective `Modify` on leaf 4; the root 3,\n261:  exclusive_bytes (L := L) (s2 := m3) (by decide) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r6).2.1.base.1\n270:example : Repr tk L0 e12 m12z := by decide\n272:/-- Each clause of `Repr` rejects a wrong MM-02 state: a usable root with a dead allocation; a\n275:example : ¬ Repr tk L e3 (m3.dealloc 1) := by decide\n276:example : ¬ Repr tk L e15 (m12.dealloc 4) := by decide\n278:example : LayoutWF Lsh e1 m1 ∧ ¬ Repr tk Lsh e1 m1 := by decide\n279:example : ¬ Repr (fun f => 200 + f) L e1 m1 := by decide\n280:example : ¬ Repr tk L e16 m12 ∧ ¬ Repr tk L f13 m12 := by decide\n284:fresh allocation satisfies `LayoutWF` but not `Repr` (two roots, one allocation). -/\n290:example : LayoutWF L2 e12b m12b ∧ ¬ Repr tk L2 e12b m12b := by decide\n294:allocation 5 of 7 stays live; deallocating it too breaks `Repr` (clause `leaked`). -/\n303:example : Repr tk La ao13 na13 ∧ Repr tk La af14 na14 := by decide\n305:example : ¬ Repr tk La af14 (na14.dealloc 5) := by decide\n335:  r1_read3 (tok := tk) (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).1 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).2.1.nd\n347:6 stays live, as the clause `leaked` asks; deallocating it too breaks `Repr` (report, (c) 4). -/\n350:example : AllOk C obR obW m12 (exitOps L tk e12) ∧ Repr tk L eX (exec m12 (exit